Date:   Sun Oct 4 10:17:57 2026 +0000

    Pick PreToolUse memories by nearest enclosing scope (hill climb round 2, tests pending)
    
    The file hook took its 5 memories by score, so a memory about a sibling
    file (same proximity as the directory) or a high-criticality
    project-wide hazard took every slot from the directory's own
    conventions. It now takes a pool of 25 and keeps the nearest enclosing
    scopes first: the file, its directory, then each ancestor; sibling-file
    and root-wide scopes last; score orders within a depth. Body previews
    follow the caller's ranking, which for the other hooks is still score.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Wgfo8G35EfHSR9QqdqvxwL

